pref-section = Organizer
pref-show-works =
    .label = Show the works behind the annotations
pref-show-works-hint = On: the annotation view lists works with their annotations (Zotero default). Off: only annotations assigned to the category are shown (like the Knowledge tab in Citavi).

prefs-citing-heading = Citing in Word and LibreOffice
prefs-citation-only =
    .label = Insert citation only by default
prefs-citation-only-description =
    When inserting annotations, insert only the citation with its page locator — without
    the quoted text and comment.

prefs-print-heading = Print annotations
prefs-keep-placeholders =
    .label = Keep empty placeholder attachments
prefs-keep-placeholders-description =
    Print annotations need a file attachment as a technical carrier. With this option off,
    FlexAnnotate removes the placeholder once its last annotation has been deleted.

prefs-citavi-heading = Citavi import
prefs-citavi-import =
    .label = Import quotations without a file attachment as print annotations
prefs-citavi-import-description =
    Zotero's Citavi import only keeps quotations anchored in a PDF. With this option on,
    FlexAnnotate creates print annotations for the remaining ones.

prefs-citavi-keep-notes =
    .label = Keep the note for the quotation
prefs-citavi-keep-notes-description =
    Zotero also creates a note for every Citavi quotation. With this option off,
    FlexAnnotate removes the note for exactly those quotations it turned into print
    annotations — notes for PDF quotations are left untouched.

prefs-citavi-link-contributions =
    .label = Link contributions to their parent work
prefs-citavi-link-contributions-description =
    Citavi knows which contributions belong to an edited book, legal commentary or
    conference proceedings. With this option on, FlexAnnotate creates "Related" links
    between each contribution and its parent work — and among sibling contributions.

prefs-citavi-locator-heading = Cite locations as
prefs-citavi-locator-page =
    .value = Page
prefs-citavi-locator-column =
    .value = Column
prefs-citavi-locator-paragraph =
    .value = Paragraph
prefs-citavi-locator-margin =
    .value = Margin number
prefs-citavi-locator-other =
    .value = Other
prefs-citavi-locator-description =
    Citavi's page type on the left, the citation locator on the right. CSL has no locator
    for margin numbers — depending on the citation style, “paragraph”, “opus” or
    “column” fits.
